.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH rqx-plan 1  "plan " 
.SH NAME
rqx\-plan \- Rank the work by what it buys against what it costs, and say what the health score would be after it
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrqx plan\fR [\fB\-\-level\fR] [\fB\-\-budget\fR] [\fB\-\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-simulate\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-threads\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-tui\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-mouse\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-motion\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-progress\fR] [\fB\-\-progress\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIPATH\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Rank the work by what it buys against what it costs, and say what the health score would be after it
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-level\fR \fI<LEVEL>\fR
relaxed, standard, strict or pristine
.TP
\fB\-\-budget\fR \fI<BUDGET>\fR
Effort points to spend. Without it the plan is the top items by value
.TP
\fB\-\-limit\fR \fI<LIMIT>\fR [default: 20]
How many items to rank when no budget is given
.TP
\fB\-\-simulate\fR
Also print what the plan does to the grade of every file
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit one JSON object per item instead of the reader\*(Aqs plan
.TP
\fB\-\-threads\fR \fI<N>\fR
Worker threads. Defaults to the machine\*(Aqs parallelism
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<FILE>\fR
Read settings from this file, layered over any `rqx.yaml` found
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-tui\fR
Never open the interactive interface; bare `rqx` prints the report instead
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-mouse\fR
Leave the mouse to the terminal. The session never captures it; the flag is still accepted so an existing invocation keeps working
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
When to colour output; `auto` follows NO_COLOR and whether stdout is a terminal
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-motion\fR \fI<MOTION>\fR [default: on]
Animation in the interactive interface
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
on
.IP \(bu 2
off
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-progress\fR
Do not draw the progress bar on stderr; `\-\-quiet` implies it
.TP
\fB\-\-progress\fR \fI<PROGRESS>\fR [default: auto]
How a scan reports progress on stderr; `plain` prints a line every two seconds for a job log
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto: A bar on a terminal, nothing in CI or when stderr is redirected
.IP \(bu 2
bar: A bar whenever stderr is a terminal, CI included
.IP \(bu 2
plain: A line on stderr every two seconds and at each phase, for a job log
.IP \(bu 2
none: Nothing
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fIPATH\fR] [default: .]

.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  rqx plan \-\-budget 20                the best twenty points of work
  rqx plan \-\-simulate                 the score each step would leave
